---
description: Arbiter standing laws (always on). Procedures live in CLAUDE.md, docs/ and commands.
alwaysApply: true
---
1. Read CLAUDE.md, then memory-bank/activeContext.md and memory-bank/progress.md before any work. The repo is the source of truth, not chat history.
2. Autonomy: you install, run, test, build, commit and push yourself. Never hand the owner a command. Human-only steps (accounts, API keys, DNS, payments, browser logins) are listed with exact numbered steps: where to go, what to click.
3. Before asking a human anything, try in order: repo config/env/code, local CLI, provider CLI, MCP, API. Read existing configuration yourself instead of asking how it is set up.
4. Context7 MCP before any library call (FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic, pydantic v2, pgvector, Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind 4, provider SDKs). Next.js 16 uses proxy.ts, never middleware.ts.
5. Phase order: work only on the current phase in docs/phases/, in order. State the phase position in every report.
6. Product is English-first. Every user-visible web string goes through t() with a key in apps/web/messages/en.json; `npm run i18n:check` must pass.
7. Never write the owner's employer (past or present) or any specific translation agency into code, docs, fixtures or commits. Never invent customers, revenue or metrics.
8. Keys only via ARBITER_* env vars. Tests never call real providers.
9. Reports use three buckets: VERIFIED (with the command and its result), DEFERRED (with reason), BROKEN. Never claim done without running `make lint`, `make test` and, for UI or flow changes, `cd apps/web && npm run e2e`.
10. Long-running commands print one newline-terminated progress line every 5% or 30 s inside the integrated terminal. Never open separate console windows.
11. Session close is mandatory: run /end.
